# launch_kit.kedi — a "product launch kit" generator.
#
# `make_kit` issues FIVE independent LLM calls (name, tagline, tweet, personas, risk). Each `>>`
# line is its own model round-trip and reads only <idea> — none depends on another — so under the
# parallel engine all five overlap and the procedure waits ~one round-trip instead of five. The
# `=` return is where the five results are awaited (after all five have been issued).
#
# `idea` is supplied by the caller as a runtime global (see run_launch_kit.py).

@make_kit(idea: str) -> str:
  >> Invent one short, brandable product name (one or two words, no explanation) for <idea>. Name: [name: str].
  >> Write one punchy value-proposition tagline (max 12 words) for <idea>. Tagline: [tagline: str].
  >> Write a two-sentence launch tweet with one tasteful emoji for <idea>. Tweet: [tweet: str].
  >> List exactly three distinct target-customer personas, comma-separated, for <idea>. Personas: [personas: str].
  >> State the single biggest adoption risk for <idea> in one sentence. Risk: [risk: str].
  = NAME: <name> // TAGLINE: <tagline> // TWEET: <tweet> // PERSONAS: <personas> // RISK: <risk>

= <make_kit(idea)>
